{% doc %}
  Checks whether a push endpoint URL points at a known Web Push service.
  The server POSTs to whatever endpoint is stored on a subscription, so
  accepting arbitrary URLs would let any user make the instance send
  requests to hosts of their choosing (SSRF).

  Allowed hosts:
    - fcm.googleapis.com, android.googleapis.com (Chrome, Edge on Android, Opera, Brave, Samsung Internet)
    - *.push.services.mozilla.com (Firefox)
    - *.push.apple.com (Safari)
    - *.notify.windows.com (Edge on Windows)

  The URL must be https, with no explicit port or userinfo, and contain no
  whitespace. To allow additional push services, override this file in
  app/modules/push_notifications/public/lib/helpers/endpoint_allowed.liquid.

  @param {string} endpoint - Push service endpoint URL
  @returns {boolean} true when the endpoint host is on the allow-list
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  if endpoint == blank
    return false
  endif

  assign normalized = endpoint | downcase
  assign allowed = normalized | matches: '\Ahttps:\/\/(fcm\.googleapis\.com|android\.googleapis\.com|([a-z0-9-]+\.)*(push\.services\.mozilla\.com|push\.apple\.com|notify\.windows\.com))\/\S*\z'

  if allowed == true
    return true
  endif

  return false
%}
